  tut1T:'The board and the goal', tut1D:'You play White. All 15 of your checkers start on the “head” — point 24, top right. Black starts on 12. Both sides move counter-clockwise: White goes right-to-left along the top, then left-to-right along the bottom. Bring all checkers home (points 1–6, bottom right) and bear them off before your opponent.',
  tut2T:'Your first move', tut2D:'Roll the dice — you will get 5 and 3. Each die is a separate move of that many points. Only one checker may leave the head per turn, so play both dice with the same checker: tap the checker on 24 — the gold spot is both dice together (5+3).',
  tut3T:'Doubles', tut3D:'Equal dice are played four times. Roll — you get 4 and 4: make four moves of 4 points with any checkers (still only one from the head).',
  tut4T:'Taken points', tut4D:'There is no hitting in long nardy, and you cannot land on a point your opponent holds. Roll 3 and 1: the checkers on point 18 cannot move — points 17 and 15 are taken by Black. Play with other checkers.',
  tut5T:'Bearing off', tut5D:'Once all 15 checkers are home (points 1–6) you bear them off. Roll 6 and 2: tap the checker on 6 and then the tray on the right, then do the same with a checker on 2.',
